  "reference": "Power aggregates ignore ghosted points. Same twelve physicians as funnel_oe_physician_power, with the smallest-volume one excluded (input index 2, which the funnel sort moves to position 1). An excluded point is hidden from signal detection entirely, so it is not among the points the chart could flag and must not colour how much reach the chart is reported to have: n_underpowered drops from 8 to 7 and the median detectable O/E from 2.3049 to 2.0697. The ghosted row keeps its own min_detectable_oe and CI \u2014 those describe the point, not the chart \u2014 and the center line shifts to 1.156187 because the excluded physician also leaves the pooled baseline. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
